p: 82%; left: 70%` and `rounded-full` inner ring\n2. **CollectionShowcase.js** - Add different color for On Sale collection\n3. **admin/page.js** - Remove the guards that prevent On Sale collection from being reordered\n\nFor the admin page, I also need to update the `saveOrder` to also save the sort_order for the On Sale collection. Currently it filters it out with `!item._isOnSale`. I need to save all items including the On Sale one.\n\nActually wait - the On Sale collection doesn't have a real DB row for its reorderable position (it's a synthetic entry). So saving its sort_order wouldn't do anything meaningful to the DB. The user just wants it to be reorderable in the UI list. Since it's the first item in the array, the order is tracked by the array position in state. I should update `saveOrder` to save all items (including On Sale), but the On Sale entry's sort_order would be saved to the actual DB row.\n\nWait, let me re-read the code. The On Sale collection has `id: ON_SALE_COLLECTION_ID` which is `00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001`. The SQL migration inserts a real row with this ID. So saving its sort_order will work.\n\nLet me update the code:\n1. Remove `filter((item) => !item._isOnSale)` from `saveOrder` so it saves all items including on-sale\n2. Drop the guard on drag-and-drop `if (src === 0 || targetIndex === 0) return;`\n3. Drop the guard on arrow keys `if (idx === 1) return` and `if (idx === 0) return`\n4. In the UI, remove `_isOnSale` from disabling drag/buttons\n5. Add red color to the title in CollectionShowcase\n\nLet me do all these changes now."},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_qCdFISOHrut0X9qtvEjz7855","content":"Edit applied successfully."},{"role":"user","content":"What did we do so far?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"<｜｜DSML｜｜tool_calls>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜invoke name=\"read\">\n<｜｜DSML｜｜parameter name=\"offset\" string=\"false\">80</｜｜DSML｜｜parameter>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜parameter name=\"filePath\" string=\"true\">C:\\Users\\Joe\\Downloads\\Magazi